---
alwaysApply: true
---

# Use Bun.js as default runtime & package manager

rules:
  - "Default to Bun as the JavaScript runtime."
  - "Use `bun install` instead of npm/yarn/pnpm."
  - "Use `bun run <script>` for scripts."
  - "Use `bun test` when writing or running tests."
  - "When generating server code, use Bun APIs instead of Node APIs unless user requests otherwise."
  - "Generated package.json scripts should use bun, not npm."
  - "Prefer the Bun stdlib (fetch, WebSocket, file I/O) when possible."
  - "Avoid Node-specific imports (fs, path, http) unless necessary; suggest `import { file } from 'bun'` equivalents."
  - "When suggesting dependencies, ensure they work with Bun."
  - "When writing Dockerfiles, base images should support Bun."
  - "If user code references Node-only modules, automatically suggest Bun alternatives."
  - "Use `bunx <package>` instead of `npx <package>` for running binaries."

project_prompts:
  - title: "Use Bun everywhere"
    description: "This is a Bun-based project. Always use Bun commands and runtime."
    examples:
      - "run dev server using `bun run dev`"
      - "install deps using `bun install`"
      - "run package binaries using `bunx <package>`"
      - "write scripts for Bun, not Node"
